    "closedAt": "2024-10-28T19:42:46Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid I understand only part of the question.\r\n\r\n> I would like to keep the visual selection after commenting (out) a block of code.\r\n\r\nSo you'd like to have it in Visual mode like this:\r\n- If text is made comment, then preserve visual selection.\r\n- If text is made not comment, then not preserve visual selection.\r\n\r\nHaving this behavior *is* possible, but will not be officially supported. Here is a snippet:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal is_vis_mode = false\r\nlocal maybe_restore_vis_mode = function(context)\r\n  if is_vis_mode and context.action == 'comment' then vim.schedule(function() vim.cmd('normal! gv') end) end\r\n  is_vis_mode = false\r\nend\r\nlocal vis_operator_rhs = function()\r\n  is_vis_mode = true\r\n  return MiniComment.operator()\r\nend\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.comment').setup({ hooks = { post = maybe_restore_vis_mode } })\r\nvim.keymap.set('x', 'gc', vis_operator_rhs, { desc = 'Comment selection', expr = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis basically overcomes the issue of determining whether the action meets the criteria for preserving visual selection (via `normal! gv`) by using custom mapping in Visual mode (via explicit `MiniComment.operator()` call which I'd personally not recommend).\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\n> Also I would not like to change lines.\r\n\r\nI don't really understand this. Could you elaborate?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid I understand only part of the question.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I would like to keep the visual selection after commenting (out) a block of code.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So you'd like to have it in Visual mode like this:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>If text is made comment, then preserve visual selection.</li>\n<li>If text is made not comment, then not preserve visual selection.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Having this behavior <em>is</em> possible, but will not be officially supported. Here is a snippet:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local is_vis_mode = false\nlocal maybe_restore_vis_mode = function(context)\n  if is_vis_mode and context.action == 'comment' then vim.schedule(function() vim.cmd('normal! gv') end) end\n  is_vis_mode = false\nend\nlocal vis_operator_rhs = function()\n  is_vis_mode = true\n  return MiniComment.operator()\nend\n\nrequire('mini.comment').setup({ hooks = { post = maybe_restore_vis_mode } })\nvim.keymap.set('x', 'gc', vis_operator_rhs, { desc = 'Comment selection', expr = true })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">is_vis_mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">maybe_restore_vis_mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">context</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">is_vis_mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">context</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">action</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>comment<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">schedule</span>(<span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>normal! gv<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">is_vis_mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">vis_operator_rhs</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">is_vis_mode</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniComment</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">operator</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.comment<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">hooks</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">post</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">maybe_restore_vis_mode</span> } })\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>x<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>gc<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">vis_operator_rhs</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Comment selection<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">expr</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span> })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This basically overcomes the issue of determining whether the action meets the criteria for preserving visual selection (via <code class=\"notranslate\">normal! gv</code>) by using custom mapping in Visual mode (via explicit <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniComment.operator()</code> call which I'd personally not recommend).</p>\n<hr>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also I would not like to change lines.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't really understand this. Could you elaborate?</p>",
            "bodyText": "I am afraid I understand only part of the question.\n\nI would like to keep the visual selection after commenting (out) a block of code.\n\nSo you'd like to have it in Visual mode like this:\n\nIf text is made comment, then preserve visual selection.\nIf text is made not comment, then not preserve visual selection.\n\nHaving this behavior is possible, but will not be officially supported. Here is a snippet:\nlocal is_vis_mode = false\nlocal maybe_restore_vis_mode = function(context)\n  if is_vis_mode and context.action == 'comment' then vim.schedule(function() vim.cmd('normal! gv') end) end\n  is_vis_mode = false\nend\nlocal vis_operator_rhs = function()\n  is_vis_mode = true\n  return MiniComment.operator()\nend\n\nrequire('mini.comment').setup({ hooks = { post = maybe_restore_vis_mode } })\nvim.keymap.set('x', 'gc', vis_operator_rhs, { desc = 'Comment selection', expr = true })\nThis basically overcomes the issue of determining whether the action meets the criteria for preserving visual selection (via normal! gv) by using custom mapping in Visual mode (via explicit MiniComment.operator() call which I'd personally not recommend).\n\n\nAlso I would not like to change lines.\n\nI don't really understand this. Could you elaborate?",
